Greetings, pilots!

We’ve got two news for you. First — no Kosovo/Serbia map today, unfortunately. We had last minute issues with vehicle behavior on this map and want to fix and slightly test them, before putting it out. We intend to update the map this week, hopefully in a day or two.

But we still decided to release the other parts of the update today. And these parts are pretty awesome: new Cobra AH-1S/F as well as several features which you were asking for. 

[img]http://i.imgur.com/sj9PFy6.jpg[/img]

Let’s take a deeper look:
[list]
[*]new helicopter — AH-1S/F, another one from Cobra family, top variant with single engine — replaces AH-64A on Afghanistan;
[*]AH-1J now has 2x2 TOW's maximum, according to real model;
[*]MH-60S, UH-60L sizes are fixed and AH-64D pilot positions are modified (thanks to s.nake for noticing);
[*]several helicopter textures are fixed;
[*]several bugs fixed (including Zuni rockets bug);
[*]new keybind mechanics: you can now bind mouse buttons and have secondary keybindings;
[*]added combat zoom-in axis, default keybindings are Numpad+ and Numpad-;
[*]combat chat fades out after 15 seconds of inactivity;
[*]Linux beta-branch (here is [url=http://forums.jetcatgames.com/forum/the-hangar-bay/tutorials-and-gameplay-guides/498-how-to-run-linux-build]how to run it[/url]).
[/list]
That’s all for today, but not for the week. Stay tuned!

[i]JCG Team[/i]

